===== PART B: git cherry-pick =====

--- 2-4 commits on main ---
$ git log --oneline main
eb61eec main: change 3
d0c29c6 main: change 2
5180894 main: change 1
65f33e0 add line2 (with -a)
ab1a34c initial commit

--- Create a new branch, add 2-3 commits there ---
$ git log --oneline feature-branch
f1942c3 feature: the important fix we need on main
0d42ead feature: work B
631eb0b feature: add feature.txt with work A
eb61eec main: change 3
d0c29c6 main: change 2
5180894 main: change 1
65f33e0 add line2 (with -a)
ab1a34c initial commit

--- Identify the specific commit to cherry-pick ---
Commit to cherry-pick: f1942c31849498614036ee8aa32571d4589b50f9  ("feature: the important fix we need on main")

--- Switch back to main and cherry-pick that one commit ---
$ git cherry-pick f1942c31849498614036ee8aa32571d4589b50f9
CONFLICT (modify/delete): feature.txt deleted in HEAD and modified in f1942c3 (feature: the important fix we need on main).  Version f1942c3 (feature: the important fix we need on main) of feature.txt left in tree.
error: could not apply f1942c3... feature: the important fix we need on main
hint: After resolving the conflicts, mark them with
hint: "git add/rm <pathspec>", then run
hint: "git cherry-pick --continue".
hint: You can instead skip this commit with "git cherry-pick --skip".
hint: To abort and get back to the state before "git cherry-pick",
hint: run "git cherry-pick --abort".
hint: Disable this message with "git config set advice.mergeConflict false"

--- Verify the change is now on main ---
$ git log --oneline main
eb61eec main: change 3
d0c29c6 main: change 2
5180894 main: change 1
65f33e0 add line2 (with -a)
ab1a34c initial commit
$ cat feature.txt   (present on main now, even though main never had the other feature commits)
feature work A
feature work B
TARGET: this is the one commit we will cherry-pick
